<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Rauracian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1792 CE – 1793 CE · capital Porrentruy</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived revolutionary republic in the Jura, the first sister republic created by the French Revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The French army occupied the northern part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-basel">Prince-Bishopric of Basel</a> in 1792, driving out the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>. Local revolutionaries proclaimed the Rauracian Republic on 27 November 1792 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porrentruy">Porrentruy</a>, naming it after the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/raurici">Rauraci</a>, a Celtic people of the area recorded by Caesar.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had a national assembly and adopted French revolutionary institutions, but it was deeply divided between those who wanted independence and those who sought union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. It depended entirely on the French army and had no real independent existence; most of its history consists of debates over annexation.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 23 March 1793 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">French National Convention</a> annexed the territory as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mont-terrible">Mont-Terrible</a>. It later merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haut-rhin">Haut-Rhin</a>, and in 1815 the area was given to the Swiss canton of Bern, much of it now forming the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jura-mountains">Jura</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/rauracian-republic.jpg" alt="Rauracian Republic" width="320" height="250"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius 12:30, 23 February 2007 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bistum-Basel2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1792 CE – 1793 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Porrentruy</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>République rauracienne</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1792&amp;focus=rauracian-republic" aria-label="Rauracian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4846 515 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Rauracian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5166 771L5166 771M5166 771L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5166 771h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5166 771h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5166 771h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Porrentruy. <a href="/atlas?year=1792&amp;focus=rauracian-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
